{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep the Sabbath.</b> And furthermore, for another reason as well, it is fitting that the Sabbath not be set aside for the work of the Tabernacle." "<b>For it is holy to you.</b> As a positive commandment." "<b>Whoever profanes it shall surely be put to death.</b> As a negative commandment, and it is not fitting to set aside a positive commandment and a negative commandment that carries the death penalty, in order to fulfill a positive commandment of the work of the Tabernacle." "<b>For whoever does work on it, that soul shall be cut off.</b> So too it is fitting not to set aside the Sabbath, for the matter of its profanation carries a severe punishment — the soul of the one who profanes it is cut off — for thereby he denies the creation of the world, and he has no portion in the Tabernacle nor in the One who dwells within it." "<b>From among his people.</b> From the rank of the souls of the people, which is of such worth for eternal life."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:40.902915528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}